From 569be0f3e8cce268477c2c5fccf84f8fdfafa5f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olof Johansson <olof.johansson@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 12:02:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] lib: sbi: add ISA-emu PMU hook + bhx PMU device

Adds a generic per-extension hit-counter hook for the trap-based ISA
emulator with a symmetric init hook:

- include/sbi/sbi_insn_emu_pmu.h declares an extension-ID enum
  (SBI_INSN_EMU_EXT_*), sbi_insn_emu_pmu_inc(), and
  sbi_insn_emu_pmu_init().
- lib/sbi/sbi_insn_emu_pmu.c provides weak no-op defaults so
  sbi_insn_emu*.c and sbi_init.c always link.
- sbi_insn_emu.c / sbi_insn_emu_fp.c track the matching extension
  through their decode trees and call sbi_insn_emu_pmu_inc() before
  each successful return.
- sbi_init.c cold + warm paths call sbi_insn_emu_pmu_init() after
  sbi_pmu_init().

Adds a bhx-specific reflection that exposes the counters via SBI PMU
platform firmware events:

- lib/sbi/bhx_emu_pmu.c implements the sbi_pmu_device callbacks and
  provides strong overrides of sbi_insn_emu_pmu_inc() and
  sbi_insn_emu_pmu_init().
- Per-hart counts live in sbi_scratch (allocated lazily by the first
  init call). Each hart re-zeros its own slot on warm-init.

Guest perf attaches with raw config = 0xC000_0000_0000_0000 |
SBI_INSN_EMU_EXT_*.
